# Source-distribution contents for AER.
#
# The wheel is configured entirely in pyproject.toml; this file exists because an
# sdist has to carry a few things setuptools cannot infer from the package
# directory alone, and `python -m build` builds the wheel **from the sdist** by
# default. Anything missing here therefore goes missing from the wheel too -- and
# the failure shows up as `StorageError` on a user's first `AER(...)` call rather
# than at build time.
#
# Two of these are load-bearing for a working install:
#
#   * `alembic.ini` and `migrations/` -- copied into the package by setup.py at
#     build time, so they must survive into the sdist for that copy to have
#     anything to copy (docs/DECISIONS.md D-054);
#   * `LICENSE` -- Apache-2.0 requires the license text to accompany the work,
#     and `project.license-files` can only collect a file that is there.
#
# Tests, docs, deploy/ and the ops scripts are deliberately absent: they are not
# needed to build or to install, and shipping them would only make the sdist
# heavier than the thing it distributes.

include LICENSE
include alembic.ini
recursive-include migrations *.py *.mako

# The build shim itself, and its own manifest: the copy step in setup.py runs while
# building the wheel from this sdist, so both have to be present in it.
include MANIFEST.in
include setup.py

# pyproject.toml is included by setuptools automatically; named here so the
# intention is readable rather than implied.
include pyproject.toml
